HST Office: a collapsed ribbon group's "Caption ▾" button is drawn as in the approved 1.0.2 mockup.

Ribbon 1.0.2 plan (phase 1, with phase 2's hst::ribbon::FoldedButtonSize and DrawFoldedButton): the button of a
collapsed group was a one-line PushButton with 24 px of padding (Đầu/chân trang ▾ was 180 px wide, its caption
below the other groups' caption line). It now asks FoldedButtonSize for its size and paints itself with
DrawFoldedButton: the large icon on top, the caption on at most two balanced lines with ▾ after the last, on the
groups' caption line, at the groups' height. Its text stays the plain caption (accessible name and tooltip).
The ribbon's group box also starts 5 px in, so the first group's content sits 8 px from the window edge as in the
mockup (panel 4 + group 4); its right end, 8 px before the banner, does not move.

